    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d437">

                <pb facs="0510" n="436" xml:id="pg436"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/1471</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Moscow</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Summers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d437-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-16T10:00:00+02:31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 16, 1918, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 1.45 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>259. Peace terms ratified last night.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d437-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Summers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d437-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d437-f1-content">
                <p>Sent via the Consulate at Vladivostok.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d437-f2" n="2" xml:id="d437-f2-content">
                <p>In the Moscow <hi rendition="#italic">Izvestia</hi>, Mar. 16, it is stated that
                    preliminary voting on Mar. 15 showed a heavy majority in favor of ratification;
                    in the issue for Mar. 17 it is reported that voting, by name, in favor of
                    ratification, was completed on Mar. 16.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
